/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-87-
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-88-### Guarded true-branch Boolean lemma
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-89-
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-90-- Extension:
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md:91:  `rule A:Bool ==Bool (A orBool B:Bool) => true requires A [simplification]`.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-92-- Class: derived lemma.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-93-- Semantic role: normalizes the final proof obligation; it does not replace
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-94-  program execution.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-95-- Domain: all Booleans `A` and `B` with `A = true`.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-96-- Matched context: exactly the displayed Boolean equality term; no K cell,
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-97-  continuation, binding, or framed state is matched.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-98-- Justification scope and context containment: when `A` is true,
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md:99:  `A orBool B` is true, so the equality is true for both values of `B`.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-100-  The guard is exactly that derivation's domain.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-101-- State footprint: none.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-102-- Value influence: only discharge of the postcondition equality; it does not
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-103-  create or change the program result.
/reference/k-proof/PROOF.md-104-- Value justification: exhaustive two-row Boolean truth table under `A`.
